INSERT INTO "journal_entries" ("id","owner","entry_on","body","source","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(1,'chris','2026-08-21',replace('Operation Better Shape – New Me — STARTING RECAP\n\nAbout me:\n- Male\n- Age: 46\n- Height: 6''0"\n- Current weight: 295 lb\n- Current A1C: 5.9%\n- Goal: lose weight and get A1C back below the prediabetes range\n- Main approach: calorie-controlled, lower-carb diet rather than strict keto\n\nCurrent daily targets:\n- Calories: about 2,000–2,100/day\n- Protein: about 140–160 g/day\n- Net carbs: generally under 100–125 g/day\n- Fiber: 30–35+ g/day\n- Water: stay well hydrated\n- Exercise/movement: increase gradually and consistently\n\nDAY 1 — AUGUST 21, 2026\n\nTotals:\n- Calories: 1,982 / 2,050\n- Net carbs: 44.6 g\n- Protein: 146.3 g\n- Fat: 129.2 g\n- Fiber: 29.2 g\n- Water: 169 oz\n- Exercise: 11 minutes\n- Estimated exercise calories burned: 116\n- Activity: weed whacking\n\nDay 1 assessment:\n- Calories were right on target for weight loss.\n- Protein was excellent and right in the desired range.\n- Net carbs were very low, almost keto-level, but there is no requirement to stay this low every day.\n- Fiber was very good and just under the 30–35+ g target.\n- Fat was fairly high, so this is something to watch over time because fat is calorie-dense.\n- Water intake was more than sufficient.\n- The 11 minutes of weed whacking counts as legitimate physical activity.\n\nOverall Day 1 grade: A\n\nMain goal going forward:\nDo not try to eat less and less each day. The goal is consistency. A successful day is roughly 1,950–2,100 calories, 140–160 g protein, 30–35+ g fiber, and preferably under about 100–125 g net carbs.\n\nUse this chat as my ongoing “Operation Better Shape – New Me” daily tracking thread. I will post screenshots or daily totals, and I want a daily recap that evaluates calories, protein, carbs, fiber, fat, hydration, exercise, and how the day fits my weight-loss and A1C goals.','\n',char(10)),'manual','2026-08-22 01:30:45','2026-08-25T15:57:01.211Z');
INSERT INTO "journal_entries" ("id","owner","entry_on","body","source","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(2,'chris','2026-08-22',replace('Operation Better Shape – New Me — DAY 2\n\nSaturday, August 22, 2026\n\nTotals\n\n* Calories: 2,164 / 2,050\n* Net carbs: 53.3 g / 125 g\n* Protein: 192.1 g / 170 g\n* Fat: 124.3 g / 85 g\n* Fiber: 21 g / 35 g\n* Hydration: 168 oz / 148 oz\n* Exercise: 7 minutes\n* Estimated exercise calories burned: 53\n* Steps: not recorded\n\nActivity\n\n* Heavy loaded carry and stair climbing: 2 minutes, 25 calories\n* Light dumbbell arm workout: 5 minutes, 28 calories\n\nDay 2 Assessment\n\n* Calories were 114 over the 2,050 target, which is a very small overage and not something that needs to be compensated for by undereating the next day.\n* Combined with Day 1, the two-day calorie average is about 2,073 calories per day, which is right in the intended weight-loss range.\n* Net carbs were excellent at 53.3 g and well below the 100–125 g preferred range.\n* Protein was excellent at 192.1 g. This was more than necessary, but it strongly supported fullness and muscle retention.\n* Fat was high at 124.3 g. This is worth watching because fat is calorie-dense, especially if it repeatedly pushes total calories higher.\n* Fiber was the biggest nutritional weakness of the day at 21 g. The goal is to consistently reach at least 30–35 g.\n* Hydration was excellent.\n* The loaded carrying, stair climbing, and 5-minute dumbbell workout all count as legitimate physical activity and gradual strength training.\n\nOverall Day 2 Grade: A-\n\nThe small calorie overage was not a meaningful problem. The main opportunities for improvement are increasing fiber and bringing fat down somewhat while continuing the strong protein intake, lower-carb eating pattern, hydration, and gradual increase in movement.\n\nTwo-Day Trend\n\n* Day 1 calories: 1,982\n* Day 2 calories: 2,164\n* Two-day average: approximately 2,073 calories/day\n\nThe overall trend remains right on track for the goal of steady, sustainable weight loss without trying to eat less and less each day.','\n',char(10)),'manual','2026-08-23 18:02:15','2026-08-25T14:40:34.978Z');
INSERT INTO "journal_entries" ("id","owner","entry_on","body","source","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(3,'chris','2026-08-23',replace('Operation Better Shape – New Me — DAY 3\n\n**Sunday, August 23, 2026**\n\n### Totals\n\n* Calories: 1,742 / 2,050\n* Net carbs: 76 g / 125 g\n* Protein: 114.8 g / 170 g\n* Fat: 96.9 g / 85 g\n* Fiber: 36.4 g / 35 g\n* Hydration: 112 oz / 148 oz\n* Exercise: 60 minutes\n* Estimated exercise calories burned: 275\n* Steps: 13,150\n\n### Activity\n\n* Church production setup — lifting/carrying equipment: 30 minutes, 175 calories\n* Lighter teardown: 30 minutes, 100 calories\n* Total activity: 60 minutes, 275 calories\n* Steps: 13,150\n\n### Day 3 Assessment\n\n* Calories finished at 1,742 for the day. This was below the 2,050 target, but it was not the result of intentionally restricting food or trying to leave calories unused.\n* Food intake was spread throughout the day with several snacks and a substantial dinner, including two pieces of homemade low-calorie, low-carb pizza.\n* Hunger was well controlled. I ate enough to feel satisfied and did not go to bed hungry.\n* Because I was satisfied and had eaten normally throughout the day, there was no reason to force myself to eat the remaining 308 calories simply to reach the calorie target.\n* Net carbs were excellent at 76 g, comfortably below the 125 g goal while still allowing a normal variety of foods.\n* Protein finished at 114.8 g. This was below the preferred range, so getting somewhat more protein would be useful on future days, particularly as activity and strength training increase.\n* Fat was 96.9 g, slightly above the 85 g target. This is worth watching over time, but it was not a major concern because total calories remained controlled.\n* Fiber was excellent at 36.4 g and exceeded the 35 g goal.\n* Hydration was actually 112 oz rather than the previously reported 80 oz. This was a solid amount of fluid, although somewhat below the 148 oz app target.\n* Activity was excellent. Church production involved a significant amount of walking, lifting, carrying equipment, setup, and teardown.\n* The 13,150 steps exceeded the 10,000-step daily movement goal and made this the strongest movement day so far.\n* Exercise calories are tracked as useful activity information, but they are not being treated as extra calories that need to be eaten back.\n\n### Overall Day 3 Grade: A\n\nThis was a very strong weight-loss day. Calories were controlled without intentional restriction, hunger was well managed, net carbs were well within range, fiber exceeded goal, hydration was solid, and physical activity was excellent.\n\nThe biggest opportunity for improvement is protein. On similarly active days, getting closer to the 140–160 g range would better support muscle retention and recovery.\n\n### Three-Day Calorie Trend\n\n* Day 1: 1,982 calories\n* Day 2: 2,164 calories\n* Day 3: 1,742 calories\n* Three-day average: approximately 1,963 calories/day\n\nThe three-day average remains almost exactly where it should be for the current weight-loss plan. Individual days do not need to land exactly at 2,050 calories. The more important goal is maintaining a sustainable average while eating enough to stay satisfied and continuing to improve nutrition and activity.','\n',char(10)),'manual','2026-08-24 00:30:35','2026-08-25T14:40:38.848Z');
INSERT INTO "journal_entries" ("id","owner","entry_on","body","source","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(6,'chris','2026-08-24',replace('Operation Better Shape – New Me — DAY 4\n\nMonday, August 24, 2026\n\nTotals\n\n* Calories: 1,860 / 2,050\n* Net carbs: 43.5 g / 125 g\n* Protein: 135 g / 150 g\n* Fat: 109 g / 115 g\n* Fiber: 40.5 g / 35 g\n* Hydration: 220 oz / 148 oz\n* Exercise: 95 minutes\n* Estimated exercise calories burned: 1,068\n* Steps: 8,101\n\nActivity\n\nMorning gym workout — 35 minutes, 298 calories\n\n* Gym time: 6:03–6:38\n* Treadmill warm-up: 10 minutes, 0.42 miles, 1% incline\n* Bar squats: 4 sets with empty bar, 6–8 reps per set\n* Hammer Strength arm/rowing workout: 25 lbs., 5 sets of 10 reps with biceps and varied rowing movements\n* Treadmill cool-down: 8 minutes, 0.31 miles, 3% incline\n* Total treadmill: 18 minutes, 0.73 miles\n* Approximate strength training: 17 minutes\n\nAqua Fit Class — 60 minutes, 770 calories\n\n* Medium-to-intense aqua fitness class\n* Included aerobics, strength, and water resistance work\n\nDay 4 Assessment\n\n* Calories finished at 1,860. This was below the 2,050 target, but I ate normally throughout the day and was not intentionally restricting food.\n* I completed two separate workouts and still ate enough to feel satisfied.\n* I had a protein shake after Aqua Fit to support recovery and increase my protein intake.\n* Protein finished at 135 g, which was very close to the 150 g goal and within the general range I am working toward.\n* Net carbs were excellent at 43.5 g and comfortably below the 125 g goal.\n* Fiber was excellent at 40.5 g and exceeded the 35 g goal.\n* Fat finished at 109 g, which was under the current 115 g target.\n* Hydration was extremely high at 220 oz. This was more than enough and does not need to become the normal daily target.\n* Steps finished at 8,101. Although this was below 10,000, Aqua Fit does not translate well into step counts, so the step total understates how active the day actually was.\n* Total structured exercise was 95 minutes, making this the most active structured workout day so far.\n* The morning workout provided treadmill cardio and traditional resistance training, while Aqua Fit provided additional cardio, muscular endurance, and water resistance work.\n* Estimated exercise calories are being tracked for activity purposes only and are not being used to increase the daily calorie allowance or treated as calories that need to be eaten back.\n\nWeight / InBody Note\n\n* The InBody scan was taken later in the afternoon after eating and drinking, so the weight reading should not be directly compared with morning or fasting weights.\n* Food, fluids, clothing, sodium, and normal daily fluctuations can temporarily affect scale weight.\n* The scan will be most useful as a body-composition baseline for future comparisons under similar conditions.\n\nOverall Day 4 Grade: A\n\nThis was one of the strongest overall days so far. Calories remained controlled without intentional restriction, protein was solid, net carbs were low, fiber exceeded goal, and activity was excellent.\n\nThe biggest success was completing both a morning gym workout and a full Aqua Fit class while still eating normally and feeling satisfied.\n\nFour-Day Calorie Trend\n\n* Day 1: 1,982 calories\n* Day 2: 2,164 calories\n* Day 3: 1,742 calories\n* Day 4: 1,860 calories\n* Four-day average: approximately 1,937 calories/day\n\nThe overall calorie average remains right in the intended range for steady, sustainable weight loss.','\n',char(10)),'manual','2026-08-25 01:14:20','2026-08-25T14:40:42.823Z');
INSERT INTO "journal_entries" ("id","owner","entry_on","body","source","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(12,'chris','2026-08-25',replace('DAY 5\n\nTuesday, August 25, 2026\n\nTotals\n\n* Calories: 1,958 / 2,050 — 92 remaining\n* Net carbs: 46.2 g / 125 g\n* Protein: 196.2 g / 150 g\n* Fat: 101.3 g / 115 g\n* Fiber: 32.1 g / 35 g\n* Hydration: 220 oz / 148 oz\n* Exercise: 48 minutes\n* Estimated exercise calories: 373\n* Steps: 9,010\n\nActivity\n\nLight Cardio and Strength Active Recovery\n\n* Duration: 13 minutes\n* Estimated calories: 105\n* Approximately 5 minutes walking on the treadmill around 3.5 mph at 2% incline.\n* Stopped the treadmill portion early because the treadmill did not feel right.\n* Followed with approximately 7–8 minutes of light exercise using 5 lb dumbbells.\n* Included various arm exercises, very light wall-supported knee bends for sore thighs, and seated couch squats/sit-to-stand movements.\n* Kept the overall intensity light as active recovery following Monday’s squat workout.\n\nTreadmill Walking\n\n* Duration: 35 minutes\n* Distance: 1.27 miles\n* Average speed: approximately 2.18 mph\n* First 30 minutes at normal walking pace.\n* Final 5 minutes were a slow cooldown, including time around 0.5 mph.\n* Tracker estimate: 268 calories\n* Treadmill display estimate: 237 calories\n* Overall intensity: light to moderate.\n\nDay 5 Assessment\n\n* Calories: Excellent finish at 1,958 calories, only 92 below the 2,050 target. This is right in the desired range without intentionally undereating.\n* Protein: Very high at 196.2 g. More than enough to support muscle retention and recovery from recent strength and activity work. There is no need to deliberately push protein this high every day, but today’s amount is fine.\n* Net carbs: 46.2 g remains comfortably within the lower-carbohydrate approach without needing to follow strict keto.\n* Fat: 101.3 g stayed below the 115 g goal.\n* Fiber: 32.1 g was only 2.9 g short of the 35 g goal. Close enough that this is not a meaningful concern for a single day.\n* Hydration: 220 oz was more than sufficient. There was no need to add additional water simply to exceed the goal further.\n* Activity: Good active-recovery day following Monday’s heavier workout. The combination of lighter strength work, treadmill walking, and 9,010 steps provided meaningful activity without trying to turn a recovery day into another hard training day.\n* Recovery: Keeping the knee-bend and squat movements very light while the thighs were sore was appropriate rather than forcing another demanding leg workout.\n\nFive-Day Calorie Trend\n\nRecorded calorie totals:\n\n* Day 1: 1,982\n* Day 2: 2,164\n* Day 3: 1,742\n* Day 4: 1,860\n* Day 5: 1,958\n\nFive-day total: 9,706 calories\nFive-day average: 1,941 calories/day\n\nThe current average is about 109 calories per day below the 2,050 target, while individual days have naturally moved above and below target. Overall, the calorie pattern remains controlled and sustainable.\n\nOverall Day 5 Grade: A\n\nA very well-balanced day: calories landed almost exactly on target, protein was more than sufficient, carbs and fat stayed comfortably within goals, fiber was very close, and activity remained appropriate for a recovery day.','\n',char(10)),'manual','2026-08-26 01:56:10','2026-08-26 01:56:10');
INSERT INTO "journal_entries" ("id","owner","entry_on","body","source","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(14,'chris','2026-08-26',replace('Wednesday, August 26, 2026\n\nTotals\n- Calories: 1,889 of 2,050 (161 remaining)\n- Net carbs: 50.7 g of 125 g\n- Protein: 181.8 g of 150 g\n- Fat: 99.7 g of 115 g\n- Fiber: 36.5 g of 35 g\n- Hydration: 132 of 148 oz\n- Activity: 65 minutes\n- Estimated exercise calories: 528\n- Steps: 7,420\n\nActivity\n- Treadmill Walking: 35 minutes\n  Distance: 1.48 miles\n  Average speed: about 2.54 mph\n  Average pace: about 23:39 per mile\n  Incline: manually varied between 1% and 3%, ending at 1%\n  Tracker calories: 284\n  Treadmill displayed calories: 293\n  Intensity: light to moderate\n\n- Dumbbell arm exercises: 10 minutes\n  Estimated calories: 81\n  Various dumbbell arm exercises with minimal rest by alternating arms or switching exercises.\n\n- Light recreational swimming: 20 minutes\n  Estimated calories: 163\n  Casual pool activity including playing, splashing, moving through the water, and some light swimming rather than continuous lap swimming.\n\nDay Assessment\n- Calories finished at 1,889, which was 161 below the 2,050 target without being excessively low.\n- Protein was excellent at 181.8 g, providing plenty for muscle retention and recovery from the treadmill and dumbbell work.\n- Net carbs were very controlled at 50.7 g and remained well within the lower-carb plan.\n- Fat finished at 99.7 g. This was notably better than several recent higher-fat days and moved closer to the goal of gradually reducing the average fat intake.\n- Fiber reached 36.5 g, slightly exceeding the 35 g goal.\n- Hydration was strong at 132 oz, just 16 oz below the tracker target.\n- 7,420 steps do not fully represent the day''s activity because 20 minutes of pool activity and 10 minutes of dumbbell work contributed meaningful exercise without generating many steps.\n- Overall activity was well balanced: steady cardio, resistance work, and light recreational movement.\n\nOverall Day Grade: A\n\nThis was a strong, balanced day. Calories were controlled, protein and fiber were excellent, carbohydrates remained moderate, and total fat was lower than the recent average while still allowing normal meals. The combination of treadmill work, dumbbells, and pool activity also provided a good mix of cardiovascular and resistance exercise.','\n',char(10)),'manual','2026-08-27 20:21:10','2026-08-27 20:21:10');
INSERT INTO "journal_entries" ("id","owner","entry_on","body","source","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(15,'chris','2026-08-27',replace('DAY 7\n\nThursday, August 27, 2026\n\nTotals\n- Calories: 1,941 of 2,100\n- Remaining: 160 calories\n- Net carbs: 66.3 g of 125 g\n- Protein: 172.3 g of 150 g\n- Fat: 97.3 g of 90 g\n  - Saturated fat: 15 g reported from 2 of 10 foods\n  - Trans fat: 0 g reported from 2 of 10 foods\n  - Monounsaturated fat: 13.3 g reported from 1 of 10 foods\n  - Polyunsaturated fat: 5.7 g reported from 1 of 10 foods\n  - Fat subtype totals are incomplete because not all foods supplied subtype data.\n- Fiber: 35.9 g of 35 g\n- Hydration: 192 oz\n- Activity: 50 minutes\n- Exercise calories: 522\n- Steps: not recorded\n\nEstimated Macro Calorie Breakdown\nTotal carbohydrates are estimated as net carbs + fiber:\n66.3 g + 35.9 g = approximately 102.2 g total carbohydrates\n\n- Carbohydrates: approximately 20.7% of macro calories\n- Protein: approximately 34.9%\n- Fat: approximately 44.4%\n\nMinor differences between calculated macro calories and tracker calories are expected because of fiber, rounding, and nutrition-label calculations.\n\nActivity\n- Hot Yoga: 50 minutes\n- Time: 5:30-6:20 PM\n- Approximately 80°F room\n- Full-body yoga involving sustained stretching, balance, mobility, core work, bodyweight holds, and repeated poses\n- Moderate-to-vigorous intensity\n- Significant sweating with noticeably elevated heart rate\n- Considerable muscular fatigue and soreness\n- Treadmill/tracker recorded exercise calories: 522\n\nDay 7 Assessment\n- Calories were well controlled at 1,941, finishing 159-160 calories below the 2,100 target without being unusually low.\n- Protein was excellent at 172.3 g, comfortably above the 150 g target and supportive of muscle recovery after a demanding full-body yoga session.\n- Net carbs remained moderate at 66.3 g, well within the lower-carbohydrate target.\n- Fiber reached 35.9 g and met the daily goal.\n- Total fat was 7.3 g above the 90 g tracker goal. That is a relatively small overage in the context of an otherwise strong nutrition day.\n- Reported saturated fat was 15 g, although only 2 of 10 foods included saturated-fat information, so the true daily amount may be higher.\n- Hydration was very high at 192 oz. The increased fluid intake makes sense in the context of a hot, sweaty workout, although there is no need to deliberately push intake this high every day.\n- Hot yoga added a substantial mobility, balance, core, muscular-endurance, and cardiovascular challenge. The 522-calorie figure should be treated as an equipment/wearable estimate rather than a precise metabolic measurement.\n- Steps were not recorded, but step count would not adequately represent this workout anyway.\n\n7-Day Calorie Trend\n- Fri Aug 21: 1,982\n- Sat Aug 22: 2,164\n- Sun Aug 23: 1,742\n- Mon Aug 24: 1,860\n- Tue Aug 25: 1,958\n- Wed Aug 26: 1,889\n- Thu Aug 27: 1,941\n\n7-day total: 13,536 calories\n7-day average: approximately 1,934 calories/day\n\nThat keeps the first full 7-day average solidly below the current 2,100-calorie target while still maintaining strong protein intake and consistent activity.\n\nOverall Day 7 Grade: A\nA well-balanced day: controlled calories, excellent protein, target-level fiber, moderate carbs, and a demanding workout. The modest fat overage is not significant enough to meaningfully detract from the overall day.','\n',char(10)),'manual','2026-08-28 11:52:02','2026-08-28 11:52:02');
INSERT INTO "journal_entries" ("id","owner","entry_on","body","source","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(16,'chris','2026-08-28',replace('Friday, August 28, 2026\n\nHydration / Ketone Check\n\nUrine color:\n- Pale yellow / light straw\n- Appearance is consistent with being well hydrated\n- Not completely clear, so this sample does not appear obviously over-diluted from excessive fluid intake\n\nUrine ketone strip:\n- Approximate result: Small\n- Closest match on the strip chart: about 1.5 mmol/L\n- This shows measurable ketones were present in the urine at the time of testing\n\nContext:\n- This was not being used to track or pursue ketosis\n- The test was done out of curiosity because I generally eat a lower-carbohydrate diet\n- A positive urine ketone result can occur with lower carbohydrate intake, exercise, meal timing, and other normal factors\n- Urine ketone strips are only a rough indicator and should not be interpreted the same as a blood ketone measurement\n\nOverall:\nHydration looked good based on urine color. The ketone strip showed a small amount of urinary ketones, which is interesting in the context of my lower-carb diet but does not mean I am intentionally following a ketogenic diet.','\n',char(10)),'manual','2026-08-28 18:13:25','2026-08-28 18:13:25');
